                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Alright. I've had a chance to play a bit into Sarab: Duji Tower at this point. I'm obviously not too far in, but I've already got a pretty clear impression of the game and really doubt I'll play it any further. It's actually not a bad game at all. In fact, as far as RPG Maker titles go, this is maybe a little above average. It handles well and includes a run option which I appreciate. The controls are simple and combat is old school turn based JRPG as are the way you simply walk into a creature to initiate combat. That said, it's not really engaging in my estimation in any regard.\n\nThe writing struggles, both from a simple translation (and/or sentence structure) standpoint as well as simply from a pretty cliche perspective. It's not bad, but it does carry all the hallmarks of \"seen that plenty of times before\" style writing.\n\nThe graphics are decent and the cutscenes seem to be well done.\n\nIt says full controller support on the product page, but I didn't find that to be the case here. However, k/m controls are as simple as the arrow keys, the shift button, enter and escape; so not such a big deal all told.\n\nI think I would give this game a passing rating. It does everything well enough and seems like a decent game. That said, there is definitely much better stuff out there to play. 5.5/10\n\n[code]If you found this review helpful and would be interested in supporting my Curator group, it would be appreciated. Cheers.\nhttps://store.steampowered.com/curator/32549618/[/code]",
